  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S.Pfizer Limited vs The Drugs Inspector on 4 October, 2024 2024:Ker:75200 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice P.M.Manoj Friday, The 4Th Day Of October 2024 / 12Th Aswina, 1946 Wp(C) No. 33521 Of 2014 Petitioner: M/S.Pfizer Limited Patel Estate, S.V.Road, Jogeshwari(West), Mumbai-400 102, Represented By Its Authroised Director Shri.Samir S. Kazi. By Advs. Dr.S.Gopakumaran Nair (Sr.) Sri.P.A.Mohammed Shah Smt.P.M.Mazna Mansoor Sri.S.Prasanth Sri.B.Prasanth Sri.P.Sreekumar Sri.Sooraj T.Elenjickal Sri.T.S.Sarath Smt.Uma Respondents: 1 The Drugs Inspector Zone-Ii, Kalamassery, Ernakulam-683 104 2 The Assistaant Drugs Controller Ernakulam-682 030. 3 The Drugs Controller Office Of The Drugs Controller Statue, Thiruvananthapuram-695 001 Wp(C) No.33521 of 2014 2 2024:Ker:75200 M/S.Pfizer Limited vs The Drugs Inspector on 4 October, 2024",
    "facts": "The writ petition is preferred by a company which is involved in marketing, distributing and selling all over India of branded product called 'Beco Special'. It is stated that the said product is a food or nutritional supplement manufactured under valid license issued by the statutory authorities. The grievance voiced in this writ petition is that Ext.P3 prosecution initiated by the 1st respondent on the premise that the said product was made without availing a valid drug manufacturing license. 2. It is the case of the petitioner that the petitioner Company is manufacturing and marketing a range of pharmaceutical products and food or nutritional supplements. In this case the petitioner is selling a branded product named 4 2024:KER:75200 'Beco Special' all over India including State of Kerala, which is a food or nutritional supplement manufactured by M/s. Geltec Private Limited, Mumbai under the PFA license issued by the Government of Karnataka under the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954. The said product is a nutritional supplement and not a drug, and its wrapper, package and literature clearly say that it is a nutritional or food supplement. The product complies with the standards prescribed for food supplements under the Nutrient Requirement and Recommended Dietary Allowance for Indians as issued by ICMR. 3. It is further stated that the said product is not covered by the definition of 'drug' as defined in M/S.Pfizer Limited vs The Drugs Inspector on 4 October, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/83933381/ 2 Section 3(b) of the Drugs and Cosmetics Act, 1940, as the same is not a medicine or drug intended for internal or external use of human beings or animals. The said product is not used for therapeutical purpose also, as the same is a dietary supplement. While so, they received a communication as per Ext.P1 stating that the 1st respondent has initiated prosecution against the company in respect of 'Beco Special' marketed by the petitioner. It is for the reason that the petitioner had manufactured and marketed drugs under the guise of food supplements without a 5 2024:KER:75200 valid drug manufacturing license to do so. It was instructed the petitioner to produce certain documents as per Ext.P3. The writ petition is preferred stating that the 1st respondent has no jurisdiction to issue Ext.P3, as the same does not come within the definition of Section 3(b) of the Drugs and Cosmetics Act, 1940.",
